      "chunk_index": 2,
      "chunk_id": "s01_c02",
      "text": "This Stanford work introduces LPLR, a randomized algorithm that factorizes any matrix into two low-rank factors, then quantizes them to low precision, compressing to one bit per coordinate while matching prior compression on images, embeddings, and LlaMa-7b we",
